{"category": "rule:ordinary", "end_line": 31, "file": "reference-semantics/semantics/builtins.k", "id": "reference-semantics/semantics/builtins.k:26", "keyword": "rule", "sha256": "96ff7b5d6842d3d84921d09065a102d30cef8965f02be8980b6c6e7bba0d9f48", "start_line": 26, "text": "rule seqLen(rangeObj(LO:Int, HI:Int, ST:Int)) => rangeLen(LO, HI, ST)\n\n  // ==== list(seq) — materialize a list/tuple into a list (e.g. list(d.keys())) ==\n  // Minimal: the \"copy a sequence\" case (list of a list is itself; list of a tuple keeps order).\n  // list() of other iterables (str/range/set/zip) is added via the iterator fold when needed.\n  // (k-cell — list() constructs a NEW object)"}
